                <div id="div_commands" class="section">
                    <div class="title">
                        <span style="margin-left: 10px"></span>Commands</div>
                    <div id="div_commands_general" class="content commands">
                        You will be provided an XML Feed URL to get full Odds data with the format as below:
                        <br />
                        <a target="_blank" href="@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml">
                            @Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml </a>
                        <br />
                        You can get list of supported sports, bet types and leagues in following links:
                        <ul>
                            <li><a href="#" onclick="ActiveMenu(div_appendix_sports, '.appendix')">Get list of sports:</a>
                                provides a list of supported sports.</li>
                            <li><a href="#" onclick="ActiveMenu(div_appendix_bettypes, '.appendix')">Get list of
                                bet types:</a> provides a list of supported bet types.</li>
                            <li><a href="#" onclick="ActiveMenu(div_appendix_countries, '.appendix')">Get list of
                                countries:</a> provides a list of supported countries.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div id="div_commands_timestamp" class="content commands">
                        <span class="sub_title">USING TIMESTAMP</span>
                        <hr />
                        To get the latest changes of Odds only, you need to specify the biggest timestamp
                        in your previous data request then input this parameter in the query string. Please,
                        note that this timestamp must be retrieved from child node only.
                        <br />
                        <a href="javascript:;">
                            @Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?t=[timestamp] </a>
                        <p>
                            <strong>Note</strong>: The biggest timestamp value is stored in timestamp attribute
                            of <strong>matches</strong> node
                        </p>
                        <div id="tamstamp">
                            <pre class="brush: xml;">
@Html.Raw(ViewBag.Odds)
</pre>
                        </div>
                        <div style="height: 20px">
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div id="div_commands_algorithm" class="content commands">
                        <span class="sub_title">USING COMPRESSION ALGORITHM</span>
                        <hr />
                        To reduce the consumption of resources such as transmission bandwidth, you need
                        to use the data compression algorithm and currently we support 2 algorithms:
                        <ul>
                            <li>zip=deflate: zip the xml stream using deflate algorithm</li>
                            <li>zip=gzip: zip the xml stream using gzip algorithm</li>
                        </ul>
                        All you need to do is input the algorithm name in the query string as below:
                        <br />
                        <a href="javascript:;">
                            @Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=[algorithm-name]
                        </a>
                        <div>
                            <br />
                            <strong>Note</strong>: In case of using both parameters: <a href="javascript:;">
                                <br />
                                @Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?t=[timestamp]&zip=[algorithm-name]
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <div style="height: 20px">
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div id="div_commands_filters" class="content commands">
                        <div id="div_commands_filters_general" class="content sub-commands">
                            <span class="sub_title">FILTERS</span>
                            <hr />
                            If you just need odds data from some special events only, you can use our filtering
                            commands to do that. This will return your preferred data and you do not need to
                            download all data at the same time. Note that you can query multiple sports/bet
                            types/countries/leagues by adding the character ‘,’ between options. However, you
                            can only have maximum 5 options. If you inputs more than 5 options, you will receive
                            an error message as below: "You can only filter maximum 5 options. Please try again."
                            <div style="height: 20px">
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div id="div_commands_filters_sports" class="content sub-commands">
                            <span style="color: #33495F; font-size: 15px; font-weight: bold">Sports Filter</span>
                            <hr />
                            You can filter odds data from the list of your preferred sports by inputting '&sport='
                            and sportID (refer <a href="#" onclick="ActiveMenu(div_appendix_sports, '.appendix')">
                                here</a> to get defined sportID). Reminder that you can query multiple sports
                            by adding the character ‘,’ between sports and the maximum options are 5.
                            <br />
                            For example: You want to query sport types: Soccer, Basketball, or Football.
                            <br />
                            <a target="_blank" href="@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=gzip&sport=1,2,3">@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=gzip<span
                                style="color: Red">&sport=1,2,3</span></a>
                            <div style="height: 20px">
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div id="div_commands_filters_bettypes" class="content sub-commands">
                            <span style="color: #33495F; font-size: 15px; font-weight: bold">Bet Types Filter</span>
                            <hr />
                            You can filter odds data from the list of your preferred bet types by inputting
                            '&bettype=' and bettypeID (refer <a href="#" onclick="ActiveMenu(div_appendix_bettypes, '.appendix')">
                                here</a> to get defined betttypeID). Reminder that you can query multiple bet
                            types by adding the character ‘,’ between bet types and the maximum options are
                            5.
                            <br />
                            For example: You want to query bet types: Handicap, Over/Under, FT.1X2, or 1st Handicap.
                            <br />
                            <a target="_blank"  href="@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=gzip&bettype=1,3,5,7">@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=gzip<span
                                style="color: Red">&bettype=1,3,5,7</span></a>
                            <div style="height: 20px">
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div id="div_commands_filters_countries" class="content sub-commands">
                            <span style="color: #33495F; font-size: 15px; font-weight: bold">Countries Filter</span>
                            <hr />
                            You can filter odds data from the list of your preferred countries by inputting
                            '&country=' and countryID (refer <a href="#" onclick="ActiveMenu(div_appendix_countries, '.appendix')">
                                here</a> to get defined countryID). Reminder that you can query multiple countries
                            by adding the character ‘,’ between countries and the maximum options are 5.
                            <br />
                            For example: You want to query countries: Austria, Switzerland, or Spain.<br />
                            <a target="_blank"  href="@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=gzip&country=AT,CH,ES">@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=gzip<span
                                style="color: Red">&country=AT,CH,ES</span></a>
                            <div style="height: 20px">
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div id="div_commands_filters_leagues" class="content sub-commands">
                            <span style="color: #33495F; font-size: 15px; font-weight: bold">Leagues Filter</span>
                            <hr />
                            You can filter odds data from the list of your preferred leagues by inputting '&league='
                            and League Name (English Name only). Reminder that you can query multiple leagues
                            by adding the character ‘,’ between leagues and the maximum options are 5.
                            <br />
                            For example: You want to query all leagues that contain "UEFA", "FIFA", "Premier League", or "SPAIN".
                            <br />
                            <a target="_blank"  href="@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=gzip&league=UEFA,FIFA,PRIMIER LEAGUE,SPAIN">@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=gzip<span
                                style="color: Red">&league=UEFA,FIFA,Premier League,SPAIN</span></a>
                            <div style="height: 20px">
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <strong>Note:</strong> You can combine all above filters into one command to limit
                        odds feed data as below:
                        <br />
                        For example: You want to query sport types (Soccer, Basketball, or Football), bet
                        types (Handicap, Over/Under, FT.1X2, or 1st Handicap), countries Austria, Switzerland,
                        or Spain), and all leagues that contain (UEFA, FIFA, Premier League, or SPAIN).
                        <br />
                        <a target="_blank"  href="@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=gzip&sport=1,2,3&bettype=1,3,5,7&country=AT,CH,ES&league=UEFA,FIFA,PRIMIER LEAGUE,SPAIN">@Model.Domain/@ViewBag.VirtualPath@ViewBag.UserName/odds.xml?zip=gzip<span
                            style="color: Red">&sport=1,2,3&bettype=1,3,5,7&country=AT,CH,ES&league=UEFA,FIFA,Premier League,SPAIN</span></a>
                        <div style="height: 20px">
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div id="div_FAQ" class="section">
                    <div class="title">
                        <span style="margin-left: 10px"></span>FAQs</div>
                    <div class="content">
                        <strong>How often can I refresh your odds?</strong>
                        <br />
                        You are able to make calls for any changes to the feed every five (5) seconds.
                        <br />
                        <br />
                        <strong>Is my odds data delayed or real time? In addition, what is the delay time?</strong>
                        <br />
                        Your odds data is delayed 120 seconds.
                        <br />
                        <br />
                        <strong>Can I access the XML Odds Feed data anywhere?</strong>
                        <br />
                        You can only access the XML Odds Feed data in the whitelist of IPs that you have
                        registered with your administrator.
                        <br />
                        <br />
                        <strong>What time zone is used for the feed?</strong>
                        <br />
                        All times displayed in the feed are in GMT-4.
                        <br />
                        <br />
                        <strong>Other Questions?</strong>
                        <br />
                        If you have any questions regarding the implementation of our XML Feed please email
                        <a href="mailto:@ViewBag.ContactEmail">@ViewBag.ContactEmail</a>
                        <br />
                        Please ensure you include as much details as possible about the issue, such as:
                        <ul>
                            <li>Your client ID used for the XML request</li>
                            <li>Date and time (including time zone information)</li>
                            <li>Request made</li>
                            <li>Response XML output</li>
                            <li>Screen shot</li>
                        </ul>
                        This will help us provide a quick and accurate response.
                        <br />
                        <br />
                        <strong>Note:</strong> a working knowledge of XML is required, we do not provide
                        technical implementation assistance.
                    </div>
                    <div style="height: 20px">
                    </div>
                </div>
